{
    "background_story": "Sailor was a charismatic young musician who traveled the world, sharing his love of music with every community he encountered. Wherever he went, he'd pick up his guitar and sing scolions - traditional Scottish songs that told stories of love, loss, and everyday life. His soulful voice and infectious enthusiasm drew people in, and soon he'd have crowds gathered around him, singing along to the familiar tunes. As he wandered from town to town, Sailor collected new songs and stories, weaving them into his performances. His music became a thread that connected people across cultures and continents. Sailor's passion for scolions not only preserved a piece of Scottish heritage but also brought joy and a sense of community to all who listened.",
